# Root Hints — How to Download and Maintain

The root hints file (`root.hints`) tells Unbound where the 13 root DNS server clusters are.
Unbound cannot start without this file.

## Initial Download

```bash
curl -o /opt/homebrew/etc/unbound/root.hints \
     https://www.internic.net/domain/named.cache
```

## Initialise the DNSSEC Trust Anchor

After placing the config file and root hints, initialise the DNSSEC trust anchor:

```bash
sudo /opt/homebrew/sbin/unbound-anchor -a /opt/homebrew/etc/unbound/root.key
```

This downloads the IANA root trust anchor (KSK) and writes it to `root.key`.
Unbound will maintain this file automatically going forward.

## Automatic Monthly Update via cron

The root hints file is updated by IANA infrequently, but it is good practice to refresh
it monthly:

```bash
# Add a monthly cron job (as root or the user that runs Unbound):
(crontab -l 2>/dev/null; echo "0 3 1 * * curl -sS -o /opt/homebrew/etc/unbound/root.hints https://www.internic.net/domain/named.cache && brew services restart unbound") | crontab -
```

## Verification

After downloading, verify Unbound's configuration is valid:

```bash
/opt/homebrew/sbin/unbound-checkconf /opt/homebrew/etc/unbound/unbound.conf
```

Expected: `unbound-checkconf: no errors in /opt/homebrew/etc/unbound/unbound.conf`
